course: dictionary
lesson: 5135
title: Invisible things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Invisible» means not able to be seen. Read the sentence and look for clues: «You smell cookies baking from the other room because tiny invisible bits of the cookies have floated through the air.» You cannot see those bits, but your nose finds them, so invisible means you cannot see something.
explain: Some things are invisible, but we can still see what they do. Air is invisible, yet we see leaves blow in the wind. Germs are too small to see without a microscope, yet they can make us ill. So ask yourself: can I see the thing, or only its effects?
explain: The word can also mean hidden or not noticed by others. «A child who is left out may feel invisible.» Nobody can see the child's feelings, and nobody is looking at them. Here invisible means being ignored, not being able to be seen with your eyes.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Steam is invisible: the white cloud above a kettle is tiny droplets.» If you put "not able to be seen" in place of invisible, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: «Invisible» means not able to be seen.
fact: «Invisible» can also mean hidden or not noticed by others.
fact: Air, many gases, germs without a microscope, and magnetic forces are invisible, but we can see what they do.
fact: Carbon monoxide is an invisible gas with no smell, which is why homes have alarms to warn us.
fact: Phrases you may meet: invisible ink, the invisible man, feel invisible, almost invisible.
exercise: «You smell cookies baking from the other room because tiny invisible bits of the cookies have floated through the air.» What does invisible mean here? | Very loud | *Not able to be seen | Sweet to taste | Very hot
exercise: Which of these things is invisible? | A big black cat | *Air | A brick wall | A red bus
exercise: «A child who is left out may feel invisible.» What does feel invisible mean? | Feel like a superhero with a cloak | Feel too hot to move | *Feel as if nobody notices you | Feel very tall and strong
test: «Steam is invisible: the white cloud above a kettle is tiny droplets.» What is the white cloud above a kettle? | *Tiny droplets | Dust from the table | Smoke from a fire | A solid ice cube
test: «It sends the numbers by invisible radio waves to the nearest phone mast.» What does the phone send the numbers by? | A wire running up the roof | Shouting into the air | *Invisible radio waves | A long piece of string
exam: A wizard uses a cloak to make himself invisible. What does invisible mean? | *Not able to be seen | Very tall | Covered in mud | Easy to hear
